§ `Project-local daydate override`

-- A deliberately INCOMPATIBLE project-root override of the embedded `daydate`
-- library: it offers `Days in month` at one arity only, where the embedded copy
-- also offers a two-argument (month, year) form.
--
-- The embedded `actus-schedule` library applies `Days in month` to two
-- arguments. So this file is a probe: if the embedded importer is type-checked
-- against THIS copy — as LIBRARY-RESOLUTION-SHADOW-SPEC's Option B′ ordering
-- says it must be, project root outranking the embedded stdlib for every
-- importer alike — the arity mismatch is reported. If the embedded importer
-- quietly kept using the embedded `daydate` instead, nothing would be reported
-- and one module name would be bound to two different sources in a single
-- build.
--
-- See ../../../Main.hs, "an embedded library sees the project-local override
-- too".

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Days in month` MEANS n PLUS 1000
